{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "19", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "20", "S": "59"}}, "news": [{"title": "Prayagraj civic body approves land bank, fee hikes, reforms", "para": "Prayagraj Municipal Corporation will prepare its own land bank for future city projects.  A 150% fee will be charged for illegal possession of municipal shops.  Unipoles and LED displays will be installed at key transport hubs for revenue.  A one-time fee of Rs 1,000 is approved for delayed property mutation.  A committee will examine faulty electrical equipment purchased since 2023.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/prayagraj-civic-body-approves-land-bank-fee-hikes-reforms/134347190?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-85610/134347190.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Chandigarh's amended master plan gives industrial areas more space, more uses", "para": "Chandigarh's industrial areas are on the brink of a remarkable overhaul thanks to upcoming development strategies. Amended Master Plans will permit enhanced construction within current industrial zones. Mixed-use developments may emerge in Phase III areas, fostering new economic activities. Alongside, a revamped industrial policy will present financial incentives and utility benefits to attract businesses. These initiatives are designed to amplify investment and refresh the city's industrial environment.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/chandigarhs-amended-master-plan-gives-industrial-areas-more-space-more-uses/134347103?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-328474/134347103.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Tamil Nadu RERA not civil court to decide title dispute: Madras HC", "para": "The Madras High Court clarified that TNRERA registrations do not interfere with civil title disputes, which must be handled by qualified civil courts. The court denied a request to overturn the TNRERA registration for a Tambaram property, citing the project's progress in construction. Consequently, the challenge against the registration has been resolved, upholding the registration's validity.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/rera/tamil-nadu-rera-not-civil-court-to-decide-title-dispute-madras-hc/134346859?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-229026/134346859.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "rera"}]}